00:58:20,869 --> 00:58:26,869
Underworld is a 2003 action horror film directed by Len Wiseman in his feature film directorial debut, from
a screenplay by Danny McBride, based on a story by Kevin Grevioux, Wiseman, and McBride.

12
01:03:39,130 --> 01:03:45,130
The film stars Kate Beckinsale, Scott Speedman, Michael
Sheen, Shane Brolly, Erwin Leder, and Bill Nighy.

13
01:08:57,391 --> 01:09:03,391
The plot centers on the secret history of vampires and lycans (an
abbreviated form of lycanthrope, which means werewolf).

14
01:14:15,652 --> 01:14:21,652
The main plot revolves around Selene (Beckinsale), a
vampire Death Dealer hunting Lycans.

15
01:19:33,913 --> 01:19:39,913
She finds herself attracted to a human, Michael Corvin
(Speedman), who is being targeted by the Lycans.

16
01:24:52,173 --> 01:24:58,173
After Michael is bitten by a Lycan, Selene must decide whether to do her
duty and kill him or go against her clan and save him.

17
01:30:10,434 --> 01:30:16,434
Underworld premiered at the Grauman's Chinese Theatre in Los Angeles, California on September 15,
2003, and was released in the United States on September 19, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

18
01:35:28,695 --> 01:35:34,695
The film received generally negative reviews from critics.

19
01:40:46,956 --> 01:40:52,956
A surprise hit, the film grossed over $95 million worldwide against a
production budget of $22 million and originated a franchise.

20
01:46:05,217 --> 01:46:11,217
The film was followed by Underworld: Evolution in 2006.

21
